<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bahrain</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bahrain is an island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a>. In antiquity it was probably part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dilmun">Dilmun</a>, a trading centre that linked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a> valley in the time of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a>. In the early modern period it was disputed between Iranian and Portuguese, then Arab, powers, and Safavid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> held it for much of the seventeenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bahrain.jpg" alt="Bahrain" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Source: Drawn by SKopp, rewritten by Zscout370 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Bahrain.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
